{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'MC13|MC14|MC15|MC16|MC17|MC18|MC28|P05|G4|G5|G14|G18' MISSION_CONTROL.md docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md data/accounting-master/next-plan.md\"","aggregated_output":"data/accounting-master/next-plan.md:5:Next eligible phase: P05.\ndata/accounting-master/next-plan.md:10:| P00 — Verify the accepted baseline | accepted_internal | All G1–G18 retain work; bounded reference checks do not establish accounting or forecast validity. |\ndata/accounting-master/next-plan.md:12:| P02 — Complete the bounded Apple case preparation | accepted_internal | The previous structured review returned AGREE, but its process record reports timeout; supervisor acceptance remains pending.; Complete note semantics, remaining indentures, series certificates and omitted instruments remain unresolved through specific recorded source routes.; Historical retained-byte availability and whole-document representation equivalence remain unestablished.; Debt/swap allocation, noncash movements, asset cohorts and contingent outcomes remain unidentified.; Selected identities do not establish full accounting validity, empirical forecast validity or human acceptance. All G1–G18 retain wider obligations.; Two temporary-file tests could not be independently rerun in this read-only environment; their passing status relies on the matching supervisor check record and inspected test code.; Complete agreement semantics, remaining indentures, series certificates and omitted instruments remain unresolved through specific recorded source routes.; Historical availability of retained bytes and whole-document representation equivalence remain unestablished.; Selected reconciliations establish neither full-company accounting validity nor empirical forecast validity. Human acceptance remains pending; all G1–G18 retain wider obligations.; This review changed no files. |\ndata/accounting-master/next-plan.md:14:| P04 — Implement reconstruction and numerical operations | accepted_internal | Independent acceptance remains pending; the previous timed-out review does not establish acceptance.; Arbitrary-history completeness, nonlinear inference, continuous probabilistic inference, unbounded integer search and general aggregation equivalence remain unsupported.; Accounting validity, empirical forecast validity and human acceptance remain unestablished. MC01–MC35 and G1–G18 retain wider obligations.; Four P04 checker tests and two P03 checker tests were not independently rerun in this read-only review; their passing status relies on matching recorded checks and inspected test code.; Template discovery, arbitrary-history completeness, nonlinear inference, continuous probabilistic inference, unbounded integer search and general aggregation equivalence remain unsupported.; Admission records do not establish evidence truth or professional accounting eligibility.; Accounting validity, empirical forecast validity and human acceptance remain unestablished; MC01–MC35 and G1–G18 retain wider obligations.; This review changed no files. |\ndata/accounting-master/next-plan.md:15:| P05 — Execute the bounded company path | running |  |\ndata/accounting-master/next-plan.md:16:| P06 — Enforce context, chronology and resolution | accepted_internal | The passing evidence establishes bounded engineering conformance only; it does not establish professional accounting validity, empirical forecast validity, human acceptance, or whole-program MC01–MC35/G1–G18 closure.; Synthetic fixtures and structural admission checks do not establish source truth or treatment eligibility.; This establishes deterministic engineering conformance only, not professional accounting validity, empirical forecast validity, production readiness, human acceptance, or whole-program closure.; General measurement conversion, consolidation, arbitrary calendars, continuous/nonlinear uncertainty, and empirical approximation validation remain unsupported.; The default sandbox temporary directory was unavailable; equivalent reruns passed with TMPDIR=/dev/shm, and the recorded supervisor checker passed its required command. |\ndata/accounting-master/next-plan.md:33:    \"The passing evidence establishes bounded engineering conformance only; it does not establish professional accounting validity, empirical forecast validity, human acceptance, or whole-program MC01\\u2013MC35/G1\\u2013G18 closure.\",\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md:141:G1–G18 are mapped in the result note; the wider audit is not fully closed.\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:36:to the [initial gap audit](../design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md); G11–G18 refer\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:55:| MC01 | Account for complete annual, quarterly and semi-annual disclosure packages, including notes and relevant referenced material. U1, U3. | Define the source inventory, coverage units, cross-reference closure and disposition rules. A worked filing package must account for retained, structured, duplicated and unresolved content without treating page extraction as semantic completion. | Specified procedure; acquired-file inventory checked. Ch. 2 Apple and Ch. 3 coverage; `cases/apple/manifest.json` accounts for 121 annual pages, 13 annual notes and 10 interim notes. External incorporated documents and full semantic translation remain incomplete. G5, G11. The added source corpus now has 192 checked annual/interim files across nine issuers and 2018–2025; incorporated-package closure and semantic annotation remain open. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:59:| MC05 | Represent economic, reporting, publication/availability and system times; preserve original and revised history. U1, U3, D. | Specify original, latest-available and harmonised queries, cutoffs, supersession, calendar/interval rules and retrospective/prospective changes. Include exact annual/interim/restatement fixtures. | Specified in Chs. 2–3 and EvidenceView/Time contracts. Four publication/ingestion queries and compatible annual-minus-interim subtraction are reference-checked in `temporal.json`. Debt dates, periods, publication/ingestion/review cutoffs now have semantic rejection checks. General calendar and standards-transition implementations remain pending. G2, G4, G13. The accepted corpus records sourced filing dates for 56 reports and explicitly unverified publication dates for 136; as-of forecasting remains blocked where availability is unknown. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:60:| MC06 | Distinguish legal entities, ownership, control, group perimeter and consolidation. U1, D. | Provide dated entity/control and adjustment-book types, acquisition/disposal and intragroup examples, and rules preventing unexplained consolidation plugs. | Specified structural control/elimination model; Ch. 9 and `sectors.json` check a simplified 80% acquisition, intragroup loan and full disposal. Actual control conclusions, goodwill/tax/FX and complex retained interests need further authority and operations. G4, G7, G12. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:77:| MC13 | Drive economic events from contract state and explicit behaviour, then apply accounting rules and atomic journal/state updates. U2, D. | Specify one reference economic model, event payloads, recognition/measurement operations, preconditions, ordering and atomic transitions. Prove the stated bookkeeping invariant and separately define admissibility. | Specified Northstar economic decisions, event preconditions and operations in Chs. 2, 8. Reference journals, atomic rejection and idempotency checks pass. This verifies the bounded oracle, not a production event engine or accounting compliance. G2, G4, G6. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:78:| MC14 | Give scenarios and decision information explicit meanings. U2, P, D. | Define supported exogenous stress, observational-conditioning and intervention modes, or explicitly scope unsupported modes; enforce information dates and distinguish real-world from pricing measures. | Specified exogenous stress, observational conditioning, intervention preconditions and information capabilities in Ch. 8/Core 0. Finite conditioning, an information-date example and debt stress typing/provenance are checked; causal intervention execution and arbitrary information-policy enforcement remain pending. G6, G14. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:79:| MC15 | Specify ordinary corporate operations and accounting across periods. U1, U2, U3, D. | Provide a bounded coherent package for revenue/collections, purchases/payments, inventory/costs, assets/depreciation, payroll, financing and applicable closing/tax assumptions, with explicit exclusions. | Specified bounded corporate package in Chs. 2, 8 with exact annual/interim and forecast fixtures. Delivery, collection, purchase, payment, costs, plant, payroll, debt, simple tax and closing reconcile. Real tax/revenue/lease/FX packages remain separate work. G4, G5. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:80:| MC16 | Produce coherent financial statements, movements and supported note schedules from the same underlying history/path. U1, U2, D. | Define balance sheet, income/comprehensive income, cash flow and equity mappings, non-cash movements, closing and note relationships; supply a full set of expected outputs. | Reference-checked complete Northstar balance sheet, income/zero OCI, direct/indirect cash flow and equity from common journals; Chs. 2, 8 and `northstar.json`. Apple checks a coherent marginal financing stress only. General note schedules and report engine remain pending. G4, G5, G6. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:81:| MC17 | Represent financing instruments and their economic/accounting lifecycles, particularly bonds and equity. U1, U2, D. | Specify proceeds, principal, carrying/fair values, rates, calendars, maturities, rights and share quantities; work issuance, accrual, settlement and relevant modification/conversion/default cases under declared treatments. | Partially specified and reference-checked: Chs. 8–9 distinguish principal/carrying/fair values and work ordinary and convertible bond issue, accrual, redemption/conversion, shares and funding default. Detailed modification, early repurchase and other-basis hybrid classification remain open. G4, G7. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:82:| MC18 | Preserve joint conditional future outcomes, honest bounds and distinct failure/completeness states. U2, P, D. | Define result payloads and queries that retain branch/path dependence, distinguish sampled ranges from certified bounds and distinguish default from unsupported/numerically failed output without silent dropping or renormalisation. | Specified result cells, branch statuses, strict bound attainment and unresolved mass in Chs. 6, 8, 10/Core 0. Exact linear, joint-output and funding/default reference checks pass; general simulation/result-query implementation remains pending. G2, G3, G6. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:99:| MC25 | Specify APIs, adapters, storage, versioning, identity and deterministic recovery. U3, P, D. | Define complete arguments/results, state ownership, migration semantics, evidence/model/run identity, event idempotency, random-stream allocation and replay requirements with examples. | Specified APIs, ownership, canonical identity, migration/replay and stream keying in Ch. 10/Core 0; concrete adapter exchanges included. Reference identity, replay/conflict, stream and bounded frozen-export integrity checks pass; transactional storage, migrations and non-Z3 adapters remain unimplemented. G2, G9, G18. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:102:| MC28 | Connect the full design through complete synthetic and real disclosure cases. U1, U2, U3, D. | Supply a known-history synthetic company and a named annual/interim real package across multiple dates; trace representative notes through records, constraints, alternatives and all affected future statements. Add structural finance/sector cases before fixing the core types. | Reference cases delivered in Ch. 2: complete synthetic Northstar history/revision/forecast and named Apple annual/interim inventory, notes and conditional stress. Ch. 9 supplies sector/finance structures. Real-company full semantic closure and independent case annotation remain open; no complete Apple forecast is claimed. G4, G5, G7. Nine eight-year report sequences are now source-checked; report-wide semantic cases and executable oracles remain to be prepared. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:116:| MC32 | Deliver a detailed, readable LaTeX/PDF document that governs the intended implementation. U3, P. | Explain the whole problem, justify chosen methods, stage mathematical prerequisites, define supported behaviour and disclose open scope; connect derivations and sources to complete examples and interfaces. Preserve mathematical/source fidelity during revisions and inspect the rendered result. | Revised Version 1.2 candidate, 11 chapters plus two appendices, full cases and supporting normative files. Build, rendered inspection and baseline-preservation review are recorded in `review/author-review.md`. Human comprehension, domain review and independent implementability acceptance remain pending. G1, G2, G4, G5, G7, G10. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:122:| MC33 | Define meaningful acceptance and separate engineering, accounting and scientific evidence. U3, P, D. | Provide canonical conformance inputs/outputs, corpus/annotation rules, justified release-specific criteria, review status and later forecast baselines/uncertainty protocols. Existing arithmetic/build checks keep their limited meanings. | Specified fixtures, corpus strata, annotation/adjudication/split protocol, hard conformance vetoes and provisional workload limits in Ch. 11/`corpus-protocol.json`. Reference checks, new debt semantic rejection cases, accounting dossiers and author review recorded; the 192-report source panel now passes acquisition acceptance and independent integrity checks. Annotation protocol/schema and provisional family roles exist; adjudication, performance and release validation remain pending. G5, G10. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:123:| MC34 | Stage implementation without losing the full mission or concealing unresolved decisions. U1, U2, U3, P, D. | Maintain requirement-to-section/case/gap traceability, explicit current-versus-later support, dependency order, workload assumptions and open decisions. Re-audit after material changes and test interactions, not just individual rows. | Original 34 requirement/acceptance pairs preserved; assessments updated and MC35 added from U4. The reviewed repair plan and G1–G18 result map preserve current/later/source-blocked obligations; implementation order remains in Ch. 11. Wider mission and acceptance stay active. G1–G18. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:124:| MC35 | Complete feasible internal preparation before paid professional review and minimise avoidable reviewer effort. U4. | Allocate every residual gap to internal work or a specific professional judgment; supply checked facts, dated sources, a proposed answer, counterargument and consequences before referral. Any later engagement has explicit user authority and an agreed bounded scope/cost. Keep human acceptance separate from continued internal work. | Standing rule installed in mission/AGENTS. All G1–G18 allocated in `review/internal-before-expert.md`; debt semantic checks, three source dossiers, journal checks and manuscript corrections completed. The review brief is unsent; actual-company facts, source and implementation tasks remain internal. No paid-review readiness, spending authority or savings estimate is claimed. The eight-year corpus, provenance checks, 20 regression tests and annotation preparation format were completed internally without professional engagement. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:141:MC28, MC30 and MC33–35 without closing semantic, accounting or forecast\nMISSION_CONTROL.md:147:Use the [G1–G18 work allocation](docs/design/review/internal-before-expert.md)\nMISSION_CONTROL.md:204:records G1–G18 repairs and remaining obligations. All MC01–MC34 assessments\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:41:Requirements: MC01, MC03. Refines G2 and G5.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:62:Requirements: MC02, MC06, MC07, MC20, MC24. Refines G2, G4 and G7.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:81:Requirements: MC05, MC19, MC25. Refines G2, G4 and G10.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:98:### G14. Scenario modes and permitted information need enforceable contracts\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:100:Requirements: MC14, MC18. Refines G6 and crosses modelling/execution requirements.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:158:Requirements: MC04, MC27. Refines G2, G5 and G10.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:174:### G18. Reproducibility needs identity and replay definitions, not only fields\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:124:### G4. The first corporate accounting package is an inventory of duties\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:145:### G5. No complete filing-to-forecast reference case tests the central workflow\ndocs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md:5:active. The catalog preserves all MC01–MC35 and G1–G18, with no missing IDs.\ndocs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md:9:Tool session `78463` is running. P00–P04 are accepted internally; P05 is\ndocs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md:55:| P05 | Running: planning | Generate journals/statements from economic events; existing Northstar postings are the independent comparator, not event input. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md:67:The master immediately refreshed the plan and started P05. Generation 57 matched\ndocs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md:98:All G1–G18 remain open and `mission_complete` remains false. Bounded phase\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,90p' MISSION_CONTROL.md\nsed -n '96,109p' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\nsed -n '117,118p' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\nsed -n '1,68p' docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md\nsed -n '1,24p' docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,90p' MISSION_CONTROL.md\nsed -n '96,109p' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\nsed -n '117,118p' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\nsed -n '1,68p' docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md\nsed -n '1,24p' docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md\"","aggregated_output":"# AccDSL mission control\n\nEstablished 2 October 2026 (Asia/Hong_Kong) at the user's request.\nStatus: active mission; Version 1.2 is a repaired design candidate with checked\nreference cases. Full product, domain and human acceptance remain pending.\n\n## Purpose\n\nDesign a system that represents a company's historical financial disclosures,\npreserves economically different histories and interpretations compatible with\nthe evidence, and carries those alternatives into scenario-dependent future\njournals and financial statements. Preserve their separate conditional outcome\ndistributions or feasible sets, including uncertainty that cannot be assigned\ndefensible probabilities.\n\nThe immediate deliverable is a detailed, readable LaTeX product and method\ndesign, with compiled PDF, supporting literature and software investigation,\nprecise implementation contracts and acceptance examples. The eventual product\nis the working representation and simulation engine. A document build, a small\nfinancing example and an implemented prototype are different achievements.\n\n## Authority and origin\n\nThis mission records the user's existing directions; it does not replace new\nuser instructions or higher-priority instructions. The three original requests\nare preserved in saved session `01a0f8e0-0c0b-7332-8f7e-d6b93ce32761`, at JSONL\nrecords 10, 115 and 145. They establish whole-company history, heterogeneous\naccounting, preservation of alternative journals/outcomes, a broad literature\nand software survey, and an implementation-governing LaTeX document. The current\nrequest establishes this durable mission and a requirements-based gap audit.\n\nThe user's subsequent direction establishes MC35: complete feasible internal\npreparation before paying for professional review. The user supplied a planning\nrate of US$500–1,200/hour. This work order is binding; no estimated savings or\nprofessional engagement is inferred from it.\n\nThe [requirements register](docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md)\ndistinguishes direct user requirements from policy obligations and engineering\nrequirements derived from those goals. Python, storage engines, parser design,\nsolver libraries and a particular first-company example remain replaceable\nimplementation proposals. Designing a DSL is part of the work; claiming it is\nbetter than all alternatives is not a predetermined conclusion.\n\n## Main goals\n\n| Goal | Required outcome |\n| --- | --- |\n| M1 — Represent the historical record | Preserve annual, quarterly and semi-annual statements, notes, policies and relevant referenced disclosures, with their source, context, temporal meaning and unresolved content. |\n| M2 — Preserve alternative explanations | Represent joint families of admissible histories, journal movements, contract states and interpretations; distinguish absent facts, accounting choices, estimates and future randomness. |\n| M3 — Simulate financial evolution | Apply explicit economic scenarios and behaviour to economic state, generate admissible journal entries, and produce coherent future statements and conditional results. |\n| M4 — Handle accounting and sector diversity | Accommodate IFRS, US GAAP and China GAAP/ASBE, industry and company differences, group boundaries, banks, insurers, liabilities, capital, bonds and equity. |\n| M5 — Specify implementable methods and language | Define reconstruction, accounting, inference and execution procedures, types, IR, DSL, interfaces, failure behaviour and persistence precisely enough for compatible implementations. |\n| M6 — Ground choices in research and reusable tools | Inspect primary literature beyond the existing collection and official software, archive relevant sources, compare credible alternatives and document justified inclusion/exclusion and reuse decisions. |\n| M7 — Deliver the governing design | Produce one rigorous, understandable LaTeX/PDF argument with complete worked cases, explicit scope, source support, method details and an implementation sequence. |\n| M8 — Establish evidence and maintain direction | Define conformance and release evidence, preserve reproducibility, keep engineering/accounting/scientific conclusions separate, and maintain requirements and open decisions as work proceeds. |\n\n## Requirements that must survive every implementation choice\n\n1. Source preservation is broader than numerical extraction. Account for all\n   source material within the declared disclosure package, including notes and\n   cross-references. Content that cannot yet be formalised stays visible with\n   a reason; it is not silently excluded from a completeness claim.\n2. Preserve reported assertions, derived consequences and modelling assumptions\n   separately. A missing value is not zero; a reported number is not automatic\n   proof of the underlying economic state. Source conflicts remain inspectable.\n3. Carry entity, group perimeter, concept, dimensions, units, currency, basis,\n   precision and time through every calculation. Label mapping does not itself\n   convert between accounting standards. Avoid double counting overlapping\n   classifications.\n4. Preserve original and revised information. Economic time, reporting periods,\n   availability/publication and system ingestion/version time answer different\n   questions. Historical forecasts cannot use later evidence inadvertently.\n5. Keep alternatives jointly consistent across statements, notes, dates,\n   contracts and accounts. Include economic state beyond journals: identical\n   historical postings can conceal different future exposures.\n6. Every reconstructed family has an explicit model scope and completeness\n   status. A selected witness, bounded search or convenient aggregate cannot be\n   presented as all real histories. Scope exclusions remain mission limitations.\n7. Preserve conditional results by explanation and scenario. A set or interval\n   does not become a probability distribution without a declared measure. No\n   weights from representation counts, arbitrary equality or LLM confidence.\n   Keep dependence between statement amounts and through time.\n8. Generate events from explicit contract and behavioural assumptions, then\n   apply recognition/measurement and posting rules. Balanced journals are\n   necessary but do not prove accounting treatment or economic correctness.\n9. Treat unsupported calculations, unresolved branches, numerical failure and\n   economically meaningful default as distinct outcomes. Do not silently drop\n   failed branches, manufacture financing or report sampled extrema as exact\n   bounds.\n10. Compare a DSL with credible alternatives on the same tasks, especially the\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| MC23 | Explain the DSL's role and tradeoffs against credible alternatives, including typed ordinary code, XBRL, ledgers, rule languages and probabilistic tools. U1, U3, P. | Tie each claimed benefit to the same concrete tasks and shared semantic requirements; state costs and a fair authoring comparison protocol. Keep empirical superiority unclaimed until evaluated. | Specified shared-IR comparison and identical authoring tasks in Chs. 5, 11/Core 0; limited syntax/literal equivalence checked. Participant study, full frontend equivalence and any superiority claim remain unevaluated. G2, G9. |\n| MC24 | Specify the core language and IR completely enough for compatible independent implementations. U3, D. | Provide complete grammar/lexical rules, AST/IR schemas, types, context rules, built-ins, errors, package interfaces and source-to-IR-to-result fixtures, including the demonstration package. | Core 0 grammar, closed structural IR, built-ins, arities, context/domain rules and complete debt dependency package supplied. Authored expected IR and selected expression-to-result checks pass. A frozen 17-export registry and bounded debt static validator now pass positive and schema-valid negative cases. General compilation, package loading, remaining semantic conformance and independent implementability assessment remain open. G2, G12, G15. |\n| MC25 | Specify APIs, adapters, storage, versioning, identity and deterministic recovery. U3, P, D. | Define complete arguments/results, state ownership, migration semantics, evidence/model/run identity, event idempotency, random-stream allocation and replay requirements with examples. | Specified APIs, ownership, canonical identity, migration/replay and stream keying in Ch. 10/Core 0; concrete adapter exchanges included. Reference identity, replay/conflict, stream and bounded frozen-export integrity checks pass; transactional storage, migrations and non-Z3 adapters remain unimplemented. G2, G9, G18. |\n| MC26 | Specify supported numerical/solver operations and their limits. U3, P, D. | Define formula fragments, reformulations, exact/approximate monetary treatment, rounding, strict-domain bounds, infeasibility/conflict evidence, timeout and resource behaviour. | Specified rational-linear/finite-choice scope, amount reformulation, quantisation distinctions and typed unknowns in Ch. 6/Core 0. Z3 checks 4.975 attained and 7.035 unattained and concrete histories. Nonlinear solvers and a production rounding/optimization layer remain pending. G3, G10. |\n| MC27 | Specify analyst/LLM review and correction as a traceable local workflow. U1, U3, D. | Define proposal, acceptance, alternative, rejection and supersession actions, with evidence requirements, consistency checks and derived-result invalidation; show an actual conflict-resolution example. | Specified Propose/Accept/AcceptAlternative/Reject/Supersede actions, examples and dependency invalidation in Ch. 10/Core 0. The transitive invalidation oracle passes; a complete analyst UI/workflow and human adjudication remain pending. G2, G17. |\n| MC28 | Connect the full design through complete synthetic and real disclosure cases. U1, U2, U3, D. | Supply a known-history synthetic company and a named annual/interim real package across multiple dates; trace representative notes through records, constraints, alternatives and all affected future statements. Add structural finance/sector cases before fixing the core types. | Reference cases delivered in Ch. 2: complete synthetic Northstar history/revision/forecast and named Apple annual/interim inventory, notes and conditional stress. Ch. 9 supplies sector/finance structures. Real-company full semantic closure and independent case annotation remain open; no complete Apple forecast is claimed. G4, G5, G7. Nine eight-year report sequences are now source-checked; report-wide semantic cases and executable oracles remain to be prepared. |\n\n## M6 — Literature, sources and reusable software\n\n| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| MC29 | Conduct a broad, technically grounded literature survey beyond the original collection. U3, P. | Inspect relevant primary methods/theory/evaluation/appendices and official code where available; compare direct alternatives; make genuine backward/forward screening, source-specific omissions, corrections and claim support inspectable. | Partially repaired: 179 individual title/metadata decisions across 194 occurrences/72 searches replace generic exclusions; generation rejects unscreened candidates. Mack and selected rule sources add inspected technical support. All-candidate full-text review and later module literature are not complete. G8. |\n| MC30 | Preserve the relevant source library and precise provenance. U3, P. | Archive accessible relevant papers under the required naming convention, retain exact versions/anchors, preserve original files, and document unavailable sources without relying on their uninspected claims. | 32 catalogued paper PDFs verified by hash/page count, with original collection preserved; Apple filings and selected standards archived separately. Version/authority limits and four blocked papers remain recorded. Mechanical integrity does not certify every technical claim. G8. The additional financial-report corpus preserves 244 original versions, source/index/discovery hashes and an append-only attempt history; 192 target slots pass source acceptance. |\n\n## M8 — Validation, completion and sustained direction\n# Active checkpoint\n\nUpdated: 2 October 2026 (Asia/Hong_Kong), after multi-year source-corpus\nacceptance following the expanded-audit repair. The user directed us to do all\nfeasible internal work before costly professional review. MC35 preserves that work order.\nThe wider mission remains active; human review is not the next automatic step.\n\n## Accepted source corpus and next execution\n\nThe user's corpus-first work unit is complete at the source-acquisition layer:\n**192 of 192 target reports, 2018–2025, across nine issuers and three evidenced\naccounting families. All nine have eight consecutive complete years.**\n`target-panel-v2.json` is active and is now the collector's explicit default.\nHenkel replaces Unilever and Munich Re replaces Allianz under the reviewed\nsource-access repair; frozen v1 coverage and all original files remain under\n`data/financial-report-benchmark/snapshots/`.\n\nResume from the [corpus result](accounting-benchmark-corpus-results.md),\n`data/financial-report-benchmark/index.html`, `coverage.json` and\n`integrity-manifest.json`. QA 6 revalidated all 244 retained original versions;\nthe independent hash/provenance/grid/PDF checks pass, and 20 regression tests\npass. The old 12-, 157- and 159-report counts are historical. There are 738\nattempt/revalidation records, not 738 benchmark observations.\n\nThe collector checkpoints each attempt and supports `--revalidate-retained`,\n`--resolved-only`, sequential `--index-plan` capture and bounded host failures.\nOfficial HSBC and Midea archives, SAIC year pages, Ping An's published report\nfeed, SEC submissions and issuer-hosted US filing feeds have been resolved.\nDirect SEC archive downloads returned 403; issuer-hosted copies are used with\nthe regulator identity and filing dates retained. Run one acquisition writer\nat a time. The optional `--http-client curl` bounds total request time;\n`--source-host` can select a resolved alternate without retrying known failures.\nPing An's last ASBE slot was filled by an A-share report attachment on a public\nmirror; the distinct IFRS copy remains excluded from that slot. Do not reset\nthe ledger, initialise Git or promote source checks into accounting evidence.\n\nThe next internal work is task-specific literal/context/span annotation and\nCore 0 semantic/compiler implementation using the preserved source set and\nexisting fixtures. `benchmark-protocol-v1.json` and\n`annotation-record.schema.json` define the proposed tasks and exchange format;\nissuer-family roles are provisional, with no model score or gold labels.\nResolve incorporated documents, revisions and publication timing before\nhistorical forecasting. Publication dates are unverified for 136 of 192\naccepted reports; 56 have filing-date metadata. No paid review is triggered.\n\n## Current deliverable\n\n`docs/design/accounting-product-design.pdf` and its LaTeX sources are Version\n1.2, a 79-page design candidate with 11 chapters and two appendices. It contains\ncomplete Northstar annual/interim/revision/forecast cases, an Apple filing\ninventory and conditional financing stress, historical construction and solver\nlimits, corporate operations, sector examples, Core 0 contracts,\nreview/replay/adapter definitions and corpus/release protocols.\n\nThe 8 mission goals and MC01–MC34 retain their requirement and acceptance\nwording. MC35 adds the new cost/preparation requirement. Assessments identify\nevidence and residual obligations. A bounded debt semantic validator, frozen\nregistry and three accounting source dossiers supplement the design. Version\n1.2 corrects the Caterpillar note anchor and states separate reinsurance PAA\neligibility/recognition/timing; it preserves the prior calculations.\nControl files:\n\n- `MISSION_CONTROL.md`\n- `docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md`\n- `docs/plans/accounting-before-paid-review.md`\n- `docs/design/review/internal-before-expert.md`\n- `docs/design/review/internal-preparation-results.md`\n- `docs/design/review/internal-preparation-manifest.json`\n# Accounting master checkpoint\n\nUpdated 3 October 2026, Hong Kong, during run `20261002T233421-cea9e631`.\nThe user's create/review/execute instruction and original standing grant remain\nactive. The catalog preserves all MC01–MC35 and G1–G18, with no missing IDs.\n\n## Active run and next action\n\nTool session `78463` is running. P00–P04 are accepted internally; P05 is\nplanning. Do not launch another master or edit controller files while it is\nactive. Poll the session and consult current state before resuming. This is\na dated checkpoint; saved state and events record subsequent changes.\n\n```text\npython3 /home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/scripts/run_accounting_master.py status\n```\n\nAfter this invocation exits, resume with:\n\n```text\npython3 /home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/scripts/run_accounting_master.py run\n```\n\nThe current invocation has the configured 7,200-second wall limit, sequential\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '124,166p' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md\nsed -n '98,120p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md\nsed -n '174,192p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md\nrg --files /home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies\nrg --files data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P05 scripts docs/design/fixtures | rg '(P05/.*json\"'$|execution|northstar|temporal|p05|reconstruction_v1|apple_case_v1|core0)'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '124,166p' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md\nsed -n '98,120p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md\nsed -n '174,192p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md\nrg --files /home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies\nrg --files data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P05 scripts docs/design/fixtures | rg '(P05/.*json\"'$|execution|northstar|temporal|p05|reconstruction_v1|apple_case_v1|core0)'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"### G4. The first corporate accounting package is an inventory of duties\n\nEvidence: [initial corporate scope](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/08-modules.tex:41)\nand [report production](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex:209).\n\nSales, inventory, payroll, fixed assets and working capital are named, but\nrecognition, measurement and transition rules are not supplied as a coherent\nreference package. There is no complete company example joining accruals,\nsettlements, cost of sales, depreciation, closing, cash-flow classification\nand changes in equity. Consolidation, foreign-currency translation and\nrestatement have sound stated requirements but lack equivalent numerical\nspecifications. The tests for these operations mostly describe desired\nproperties without complete inputs and expected outputs.\n\nRequired repair: provide one deliberately bounded corporate profile with an\nopening state, event schedules, journal templates and all statement mappings.\nCarry it across annual and interim periods, including a correction and one\nperimeter or currency case. Every supported operation needs its assumptions,\npreconditions, state changes and expected reports; explicit exclusions are\nacceptable. A balanced financing illustration does not specify this package.\n\n### G5. No complete filing-to-forecast reference case tests the central workflow\n\nEvidence: [proposed demonstrator](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/01-purpose.tex:128),\n[ingestion](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex:6),\nand [example request](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/11-contracts.tex:234).\n\nThe document proposes a real company and a synthetic company but does not\ninstantiate either as a full disclosure package. There is no named filing\nset with source passages, extracted records, alternative readings, resolved\ncross-references, history constraints and resulting conditional statements.\nThe mathematical example starts after the consequential interpretation work\nhas already been supplied by hand.\n\nRequired repair: add a complete synthetic fixture whose hidden history is known\nand a bounded, named real annual/interim disclosure case. Show representative\nnotes including narrative qualifications, missing terms, a contradiction and\na revised comparative. A worked specification can be written before the\nengine exists; the gap is not simply the absence of production code.\n\n### G6. Forward economic and probability models remain interfaces\n\nEvidence: [forward equations](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/05-mathematics.tex:119),\n### G14. Scenario modes and permitted information need enforceable contracts\n\nRequirements: MC14, MC18. Refines G6 and crosses modelling/execution requirements.\nEvidence: [three scenario meanings](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/03-literature.tex:149),\n[information timing](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/05-mathematics.tex:121),\nand [scenario grammar](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/11-contracts.tex:51).\n\nThe literature chapter promises to distinguish an imposed exogenous path,\nan observational conditional forecast and an intervention. The surface example\nonly sets a driver. The record/API specification does not supply complete\nmode-specific semantics for conditioning or replacing equations. Similarly,\nbehavioural and measurement plugins are told to use permissible information,\nbut the available-information object and its access rules are unspecified.\n\nRequired evidence: declare supported scenario kinds and represent them in the\nschema. A first release can explicitly support exogenous stress only without\nclaiming the other operations. Show how a manager and an allowance calculation\nreceive current information while future simulated outcomes remain hidden.\nExplain when new observed evidence updates historical weights and why merely\nselecting a hypothetical stress does not do so.\n\n### G15. Different kinds of uncertainty need different admissibility rules\n\n### G18. Reproducibility needs identity and replay definitions, not only fields\n\nRequirements: MC25, MC34. Refines G2, G9 and G10.\nEvidence: [three identities](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:21),\n[event replay](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex:115),\nand [manifest](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/09-implementation.tex:175).\n\nThe draft requires evidence/model/execution identifiers, idempotency and stable\nrandom streams, but does not fully define canonical representation, event\nidentity, stream allocation or semantics-preserving migrations. Without these,\ndifferent implementations can assign different identities or change simulated\ndraws after a harmless branch reorder while claiming to follow the same design.\n\nRequired evidence: explicit canonicalisation and identity rules, version and\nmigration contracts, and replay examples covering formatting changes, evidence\ncorrections, reordered independent events, duplicate event IDs and branch order.\nSpecify which results must be identical and which numerical comparisons have a\njustified tolerance. No new cryptographic-attestation system is implied.\n\n/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/global-scientific-coding-agent-policy.md\n/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/scholarly-literature-audit-policy.md\n/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/humanizer-ai-writing-patterns.md\ndocs/design/fixtures/northstar.json\ndocs/design/fixtures/temporal.json\nscripts/reconstruction_v1.py\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py\nscripts/core0_frontends_v1.py\nscripts/apple_case_v1.py\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P05/plan-0.response.json\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P05/review_plan-0.process.json\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P05/review_plan-0.recovery.json\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P05/plan-0.recovery.json\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P05/plan-0.process.json\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
